diff --git a/docs/gaudi2-bf16-gemm.md b/docs/gaudi2-bf16-gemm.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..cfbb60a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/gaudi2-bf16-gemm.md
@@ -0,0 +1,108 @@
+# Native Gaudi2 BF16 GEMM
+
+`src/ops/gaudi2/bf16_gemm.h` implements one explicit static linear operator:
+
+```text
+A[M,K] BF16, W[N,K] BF16 -> Y[M,N] BF16 = A * transpose(W)
+```
+
+All planes are compact row-major. There is no bias, alpha/beta, arbitrary stride,
+dynamic-M launch or fused activation. The shape is fixed when constructing
+`Bf16Gemm(device, {M,N,K}, max_workspace_bytes)`; another shape requires another
+recipe. Dimensions must be positive signed-32-bit extents, byte products must fit
+`size_t`, and the three device allocations must match the required byte sizes
+exactly and be disjoint. This supports a BF16 weight tile produced from the
+official block-FP8 preparation path, but does not implement its model loader or
+streaming schedule. It is not an FP8-MME/W8A8 operator.
+
+## Graph and numerical contract
+
+The graph uses native `gemm`, input order `{A,W}` and
+`synGEMMParams{false,true}`. Synapse's FCD-first geometries are `{K,M}`, `{K,N}`
+and `{N,M}` respectively; there is no physical weight transpose or hidden host
+copy. All three tensors have explicit BF16 device type and permutation disabled.
+Each occupies its own persistent section at offset zero. W is an ordinary
+runtime input, not a `SetHostPtr`/const tensor copied into a recipe.
+
+The MME node explicitly requests `synRoundToNearest`. The SDK documents its
+default as round-nearest-even; the
+[Gaudi architecture documentation](https://docs.habana.ai/en/latest/Gaudi_Overview/Gaudi_Architecture.html)
+states that Gaudi2 MME data types accumulate in FP32. Output is nevertheless
+**BF16**, including its final rounding boundary. Composing multiple linears
+requires a BF16 cast after each output; FP32 accumulation does not make the
+outputs FP32. Hardware reduction order, subnormal handling and numerical error
+remain to be qualified on Gaudi2.
+
+The mapping follows the fixed official PyTorch bridge's
+[shape reversal](https://github.com/HabanaAI/gaudi-pytorch-bridge/blob/5176b1b2d6865608514e83a2b1fd66459920676e/backend/synapse_helpers/tensor_builder_base.cpp#L23)
+and [linear/GEMM parameters](https://github.com/HabanaAI/gaudi-pytorch-bridge/blob/5176b1b2d6865608514e83a2b1fd66459920676e/habana_kernels/linear_kernels.cpp#L37).
+These are interface/layout evidence, not a substitute for physical execution.
+
+## Ownership and execution
+
+Graph construction uses current tensor-handle/geometry/type/section APIs.
+Construction releases external tensor handles before graph destruction, matching
+the SDK's reference-count contract. The compiled recipe remains independent of
+those construction handles. Tensor IDs are queried by the explicit names
+`A`, `W`, `Y`; IDs are not guessed from enumeration order. Launch uses the
+current `synLaunchWithExternalEventsExt` API, flags zero and no external events,
+with actual IDs, device addresses and static geometries.
+
+The physical runtime owns the recipe and its workspace. Workspace size is queried
+after compilation and rejected before allocation when it exceeds the explicit
+budget; zero workspace creates no allocation. A `Compute` completion holds the
+recipe, workspace, stream and A/W/Y allocations until its event completes.
+Compute has its own operand/workspace leases, distinct from a completed upload's
+DMA leases. Pending uploads must first be observed complete. While compute is
+pending, operand access, overwrite, download and another use of that recipe's
+workspace are rejected. Read-sharing/concurrent launches are not implemented.
+
+The closed operator validates buffer sizes/aliasing before the private native
+launch primitive. Arbitrary caller-created `RecipeBinding` objects cannot invoke
+that primitive. `Stream::native_handle()` still requires callers to own resources
+for any external operations they enqueue themselves.
+
+Launch failure may be ambiguous: the implementation drains its stream before
+releasing leases even if the driver returned an error after admitting work.
+Event-record failure follows the same rule. Explicit query/wait failures retain
+leases. Destroying or replacing an unfinished `Compute` waits for it; a final
+unrecoverable fence/cleanup failure terminates rather than freeing active memory.
+There is no cross-stream event-chaining or compute/DMA-overlap claim.
+
+## Build and evidence
+
+The host preparation build includes `ninfer-gaudi2-bf16-gemm-test`. Its private
+fake API validates graph descriptors, persistent sections, dtype, rounding,
+transpose, nonpositional tensor IDs and bound addresses. It delays simulated
+FP32-FMA computation until an event is drained. An independent FP64 formula
+decodes the BF16 inputs and chooses the nearest BF16 result by numerical distance.
+Fixtures use exact dyadic sums to distinguish matrix/cast semantics without
+claiming that the hardware's FP32 reduction order is identical.
+
+Tests include asymmetric `M=2,N=3,K=5`, BF16 midpoint ties, a 513-term case that
+would lose increments under BF16 accumulation, and an output tile with real
+Qwen `K=5120`. They cover workspace bounds/zero workspace, partial graph failure,
+compile/ID/allocation failure, queued-launch errors, event failures, move and
+destruction lifetimes, operand reuse and later unrelated DMA. A full
+`{1,17408,5120}` FFN resource query is checked without allocating a full weight
+matrix. These tests qualify the graph/Host contract and reference semantics;
+they are **not MME hardware numerical or performance evidence**.
+
+The production runtime and GEMM source files were independently compiled against
+verified official SynapseAI 1.24.1-482 headers with MSVC 14.44 x64, C++20 and
+`/W4 /WX` (external vendor warnings excluded). Native linking, graph compilation
+by `libSynapse`, physical launch/readback and throughput remain unverified.
+
+The [native runtime build](gaudi2-runtime.md) also builds
+`ninfer-gaudi2-gemm-smoke`. On a configured Gaudi2 Linux host, explicitly run:
+
+```sh
+build-gaudi2-native/src/core/gaudi2/ninfer-gaudi2-gemm-smoke
+```
+
+It uploads the asymmetric 2x3x5 fixture, launches the real recipe, downloads Y
+and compares the exact golden values `[[17,3,11.5],[-7.5,12,-8]]`.
+The smoke is not registered in host-only CI and has not been executed on Gaudi2.
+Model-level linear binding, quantized device dequantization, GQA/GDN, full-KV and
+KVMem integration remain later work; no public Engine HPU generation route is
+advertised by this increment.
