@@ -0,0 +1,76 @@
+# GLM-5.3-Flash TPC-C kernels (Gaudi2)
+
+Ten device kernels, all compile-validated against the real TPC compiler
+(`tpc-clang 2.7.33` from SynapseAI `1.24.1-482`) with `-march=gaudi2`.
+Host bridges live in `../glm5_tpc.cpp` + `../include/glm5_tpc.h`; their
+graph/launch/cleanup lifecycle is covered by `../tests/glm5_tpc_test.cpp`
+against the fake_synapse double. Kernel **math** is verified by the CUDA
+executor tests on the 5090 host against the same reference implementations
+(`src/models/glm5/reference/`) — the TPC sources are the Gaudi2 port of that
+math, not an independent derivation.
+
+## Kernels
+
+| GUID | File | Contract |
+|---|---|---|
+| `glm5_rmsnorm_bf16` | `glm5_rmsnorm_bf16_gaudi2.c` | RMSNorm, BF16 [D,T], FP32 two-pass |
+| `glm5_clamp_swiglu_bf16` | `glm5_clamp_swiglu_bf16_gaudi2.c` | clamped SwiGLU, BF16 [2I,T] → [I,T] |
+| `glm5_kda_gate_bf16` | `glm5_kda_gate_bf16_gaudi2.c` | KDA decay gate (needs head_dim == 128) |
+| `glm5_kda_scan_f32` | `glm5_kda_scan_f32_gaudi2.c` | KDA delta recurrence, two HBM streaming passes (needs head_dim == 128) |
+| `glm5_mhc_gates_bf16` | `glm5_mhc_gates_bf16_gaudi2.c` | mHC pre/post/comb gates + 4x4 Sinkhorn |
+| `glm5_mhc_collapse_bf16` | `glm5_mhc_collapse_bf16_gaudi2.c` | pre-block stream collapse |
+| `glm5_mhc_post_bf16` | `glm5_mhc_post_bf16_gaudi2.c` | post-block stream update |
+| `glm5_mhc_head_bf16` | `glm5_mhc_head_bf16_gaudi2.c` | final 4-stream mean |
+| `glm5_moe_route_bf16` | `glm5_moe_route_bf16_gaudi2.c` | sigmoid router, noaux_tc, top-k <= 512 experts |
+| `glm5_moe_combine_bf16` | `glm5_moe_combine_bf16_gaudi2.c` | weighted expert sum + shared |
+
+Adapted lineage: Sinkhorn lane machinery and the top-k selection reduction
+from the 1Cat flashinfer-gaudi kernels (Apache-2.0); clamp-SwiGLU shape from
+abotsis/vllm-gaudi (Apache-2.0). GLM semantics (sigmoid+eps pre, 2x sigmoid
+post, comb layout src-major, original-score weight normalization) follow the
+CUDA contracts in `include/ninfer/ops/glm5_*.h`.
+
+## Toolchain (offline, in WSL)
+
+`tpc-clang` ships inside the SynapseAI `habanalabs-graph` deb — no full SDK
+install needed for syntax/type/intrinsic validation:
+
+```
+# one-time (proxy on the host side for the download):
+curl -O <vault>/habanalabs-graph_1.24.1-482_amd64.deb   # sha256 66b7f816...
+wsl -d Ubuntu-24.04 -- bash -c 'mkdir -p ~/tpc-sdk/extract && \
+    dpkg-deb -x /mnt/c/<path>/habanalabs-graph.deb ~/tpc-sdk/extract'
+
+# per-change validation (this directory):
+bash compile_kernels.sh
+```
+
+The script compiles every `glm5_*_gaudi2.c` with
+`tpc-clang -march=gaudi2 -c`; 10/10 must pass. On a real Gaudi2 host the
+same sources feed the GC packaging flow (recipe registration via the
+HabanaTools loader) — that integration is still pending hardware.
+
+## Type-model notes (tpc-clang 2.7.33 quirks the kernels respect)
+
+- `float128` is `struct {float64 v1, v2;}` — no implicit conversion to or
+  from `float64`; whole-vector math goes member-wise, MAC via `v_f32_mac_b`.
+- `float64` is 64 lanes: scalar↔float64 broadcast is implicit, but there is
+  **no vector→scalar extraction**. Per-element scalar values come from
+  scalar memory reads (`s_f32_ld_g` / `s_bf16_ld_g` with `gen_addr`).
+- `v_f32_ld_tnsr_b` returns `float64` (64 lanes); BF16 loads return
+  `bfloat128` (128 lanes). FP32 stores go through
+  `v_f32_st_tnsr_partial(coord, t, float64, count, 0)`.
+- Low-N lane groups ride in the first lanes of a float64 via
+  `*_ld_tnsr_partial_b` (zero-filled tail) and leave via
+  `*_st_tnsr_partial` — the whole mHC gate row moves in 4/4/16-lane blocks.
+- `*_st_tnsr_partial`'s count argument is the LAST VALID LANE INDEX
+  (element count minus one; 64 elements pass 63) per the interface
+  definition. The partial LOAD's argument is kept as an element count:
+  under either reading that stays safe — one extra lane reads padding that
+  the store's narrower range discards, while under-reading would corrupt
+  the tail.
+- Comparisons return masks via named builtins (`v_i32_cmp_less_b`), not C
+  operators on vector types.
+- `no_saturation_sigmoid_f32` does **not** exist here; the no-LUT path is
+  `v_reciprocal_f32(1.0f + v_exp_cephes_f32(-x))` (the LUT `v_sigmoid_f32`
+  saturates to exact 0/1 at |x| >= 9).
diff --git a/src/core/gaudi2/tpc/kernels/attn_recurrence_f32_gaudi2.c b/src/core/gaudi2/tpc/kernels/attn_recurrence_f32_gaudi2.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..d3bd17b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/core/gaudi2/tpc/kernels/attn_recurrence_f32_gaudi2.c
@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
+// Independent heads share vector instructions; key traversal stays ordered.
+void main(tensor scores, tensor indices, tensor sink, tensor lengths,
+          tensor coefficients, tensor normalization, int sequence_length)
+{
+    const int5 begin = get_index_space_offset();
+    const int5 end = begin + get_index_space_size();
+    const int width = get_dim_size(indices, 0);
+    const int5 zero = {0};
+    const float64 sinks = v_f32_ld_tnsr_partial_b(zero, sink, 31, 0);
+    for (int token = begin[2]; token < end[2]; ++token) {
+        const int5 lc = {token, 0, 0, 0, 0};
+        int count = s_i32_ld_g(gen_addr(lc, lengths));
+        count = count < 0 ? 0 : count > width ? width : count;
+        float64 maximum = -3.402823466e+38f;
+        float64 sum = 0.0f;
+        for (int position = 0; position < count; ++position) {
+            const int5 ic = {position, token, 0, 0, 0};
+            const int row = s_i32_ld_g(gen_addr(ic, indices));
+            if (row < 0 || row >= sequence_length) continue;
+            const int5 sc = {0, position, token, 0, 0};
+            const float64 score = v_f32_ld_tnsr_partial_b(sc, scores, 31, 0);
+            const float64 next = v_f32_max_b(maximum, score);
+            const float64 previous = v_exp_cephes_f32(maximum - next);
+            const float64 weight = v_exp_cephes_f32(score - next);
+            sum = sum * previous + weight;
+            const int5 pc = {0, 0, position, token, 0};
+            const int5 wc = {0, 1, position, token, 0};
+            v_f32_st_tnsr_partial(pc, coefficients, previous, 31, 0);
+            v_f32_st_tnsr_partial(wc, coefficients, weight, 31, 0);
+            maximum = next;
+        }
+        const float64 final_max = v_f32_max_b(maximum, sinks);
+        const float64 data_scale = v_exp_cephes_f32(maximum - final_max);
+        const float64 sink_weight = v_exp_cephes_f32(sinks - final_max);
+        sum = sum * data_scale + sink_weight;
+        const float64 result = data_scale * v_reciprocal_f32(sum);
+        const int5 nc = {0, token, 0, 0, 0};
+        v_f32_st_tnsr_partial(nc, normalization, result, 31, 0);
+    }
+}
diff --git a/src/core/gaudi2/tpc/kernels/clamp_swiglu_bf16_gaudi2.c b/src/core/gaudi2/tpc/kernels/clamp_swiglu_bf16_gaudi2.c
